{"text": "PHILIP MORRIS USA RECORDS MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT\n\nDate: September 9, 1994\nTo: Linda Collins\nFrom: Lewis Cummings\n\nSubject\u2019 Records Management Commendation\n\n| would ike to thank you for the work you have put forth this year on the Philip\nMorris USA Records Management Program. As you know, much of our\n\u2018emphasis this year has been in the legal environment where we have identified\nand suspended the appropriate records needed for an unprecedented amount\n\nof litigation. As a departmental records coordinator, your efforts in this regard\nprovided an invaluable service to the company.\n\nBy coordinating Records Management activities for the #Bed/Travet\nSBRVCENTEUTCING Administration Department this year, you also played a vital\nroll in helping Philip Morris fulfil its legal, regulatory and business retention\nrequirements while reducing its overall records maintenance costs. In the cost\nsavings arena this year, l estimate we will reduce our burden of maintaining\nUnnecessary active records at Philip Morris by 30 to 36 million documents and\nfiles. This translates into a net saving of nearly 2 million dollars in equipment\nand materials alone. Other benefits such as a reduction in legal expenses,\nimproved access and retrieval of information, and reduced space requirements\nwill even more dramatically increase these projected savings, Your leadership\n\nroll and the support and diligence you put forth this year were imperative to\nPhilip Morris achieving this magnitude of success.\n\n{As always, | will ook forward to continuing to work with you in our future efforts\nto help Philip Morris manage its records and information resources in the most\nefficient and cost-effective manner possible. If you should have future\nsuggestions about how we can make the program better, please let me know.\n\u2018Thanks again for your contributions and outstanding support.\n\ncc: W. G. Worontsoff y a\nFILE; RO273 \u2014f,\nLT the\n\ngpgggotsoe",
